    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="bl_d42">

                <pb facs="bl_d42-1" n="1" xml:id="bl_d42-1"/>

                <head>BL–42. Telegram from the Ambassador in Bolivia (Strom) to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="bl_d42-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>La Paz</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-12-24">December 24,
                        1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Communique from Secretary General Presidency announces 1) government USSR
                    has officially informed GOB its willingness receive in Moscow commission
                    technicians and economists to discuss A) tin smelter offer B) credits up to $150
                    million for technical assistance equipment and new installations Comibol and
                    YPFB C) possibility long–term acquisition Bolivian mine production 2) GOB has
                    reaffirmed decision ascend commission under Minister Mines discuss Soviet
                    proposals 3) commission to travel Moscow latter half January.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Strom</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#bl_d42-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="bl_d42-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 824.25/12–2460. Unclassified. No
                    dispatch time is recorded on the source text; it was received in the Department
                    on December 27, 8:59 a.m., having been delayed in transmission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
